    pr_ref:  # 8b31
    description: ""  # 8b31
    fields:  # 8b31
      statement: "The ADR-0033 writer-contract validator must read AnalysisRun records via dict-or-attribute access. Production feeds them as serialized run.to_dict() dicts (cli.py: analysis_runs.append(linker_result.run.to_dict())), so bare getattr returns the default and every writer-contract check silently no-ops on the production substrate."  # 8b31
      root_cause: "Shape mismatch between producer and validator: the writer-contract checks assumed dataclass attribute access (getattr) while the orchestrator serializes AnalysisRuns to dicts before validate_ir. The dict-or-attribute _read helper already existed and was used by the axis-conformance branch, but the writer-contract branch (sub-pattern-2 sentinel match + example_id, plus _is_truthy / sub-pattern-1) still used bare getattr. Object-shaped unit tests masked the production no-op."  # 8b31
